shes in a dashed line. Ignored if the corresponding line-type attribute is not dashed.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"spaceLength","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The length, in tenths, of the spaces in a dashed line. Ignored if the corresponding line-type attribute is not dashed."}]}]},{"name":"position","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of font names.The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"font"},{"name":"color","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveShift\/init(id:kind:number:size:dashLength:spaceLength:position:font:color:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOctaveShift/init(id:kind:number:size:dashLength:spaceLength:position:font:color:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"MXLOctaveShift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"init(id:kind:number:size:dashLength:spaceLength:position:font:color:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxloctaveshift\/init(id:kind:number:size:dashlength:spacelength:position:font:color:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveShift\/init(id:kind:number:size:dashLength:spaceLength:position:font:color:)","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL21MXLUpDownStopContinueO","text":"MXLUpDownStopContinue"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","text":"MXLNumberLevel"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"size"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"dashLength"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"spaceLength"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"position"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV","text":"MXLPosition"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"font"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLFontV","text":"MXLFont"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?)"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOctaveShift":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The octave shift type indicates where notes are shifted up or down from their true pitched values because of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"printing difficulty. Thus a treble clef line noted with 8va will be indicated with an octave-shift down from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the pitch data indicated in the notes. A size of 8 indicates one octave; a size of 15 indicates two octaves."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveShift","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxloctaveshift","title":"MXLOctaveShift","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLOctaveShift"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLOctaveShift"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLUpDownStopContinue":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The up-down-stop-continue type is used for octave-shift elements, indicating the direction of the shift from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"their true pitched values because of printing difficulty.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLUpDownStopContinue","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlupdownstopcontinue","title":"MXLUpDownStopContinue","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLUpDownStopContinue"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLUpDownStopContinue"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vs. a music font.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLFont","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Slurs, tuplets, and many other features can be concurrent and overlap within a single musical part. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number-level entity distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"MusicXML document order. Values greater than 6 are usually only needed for music with a large number of divisi"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"staves in a single part, or if there are more than 6 cross-staff arpeggios in a single measure. When a number-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"level value is implied, the value is 1 by default."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLNumberLevel","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"abstract":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLPosition","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTenths":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTenths","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTenths"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tenths type is a number representing tenths of interline staff space (positive or negative). Both integer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and decimal values are allowed, such as 5 for a half space and 2.5 for a quarter space. Interline space is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured from the middle of a staff line."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLTenths","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltenths","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTenths"}]}}}